mately 912 people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 32%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $180K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $29K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Rush Street Interactive, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.9B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +24% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +11.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","The business throws off $164M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.95\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 95\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (90% sell ratio, net $15.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 47% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 48% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Accel Entertainment (NYSE:ACEL) versus Rush Street Interactive (NYSE:RSI) Financial Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/accel-entertainment-nyseacel-versus-rush-street-interactive-nysersi-financial-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794566814.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.967,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Lori R Schwartz 2025 Gift Trust Files to Sell 55,555 Shares of Rush Street Interactive (RSI)","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/lori-r-schwartz-2025-gift-trust-files-to-sell-55555-shares-of-rush-street-interactive-rsi","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794277907.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.813,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Richard T Schwartz Revocable Trust Files 